  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b1f1002765951330b4e4c03d4989cfe1</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.8</version>
    <time>1794828484</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Prepare for configuation of the SUSE registry in the gateway
  for supervisor and sandbox images.
  Values get added once the paths are known.
- Improve documentation.

- Updated to 0.1.8.
  * Breaking changes:
    - Credential placement is stricter: static provider credentials are
      now only injected into the Authorization header or an explicit
      body/WebSocket rewrite. If you use custom headers, query parameters
      or path slots, your policy must now declare where the credential goes.
    - WebSockets need explicit config: REST endpoints now reject HTTP upgrade
      requests with 403. WebSocket traffic needs its own protocol and rules
      in the policy.
    - Symlinks in writable workspaces can block launch: a sandbox won't
      start if a filesystem policy path goes through a symlink in a writable
      workspace.
  * SDK changes:
    - Go: move from github.com/NVIDIA/OpenShell/sdk/go to
      github.com/ai-openshell/sdk-go. The Go SDK now shares oidc_token.json
      with the CLI, so run openshell gateway login once.
    - Python: still pip install openshell, but it's now published from a
      separate repo.
  * User visible changes:
    - Stability: deleted sandboxes no longer leak memory, so repeated
      create/delete cycles no longer end in an OOM kill. Kubernetes sandbox
      deletion is faster, and stopped sandboxes no longer flip back to
      &quot;provisioning&quot;.
    - CLI:
      - openshell sandbox download now works on busybox-based images.</comment>
    <requestid>1397257</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>6e99c005cbb550964c6e6c77a034897f</srcmd5>
    <version>0.1.10</version>
    <time>1795619644</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Fixed older changelogs to remove entries irrelevant to the package
  since certain features are not supported (yet).
- Update to version 0.1.10
  * Upgrade Notes
    - Application URLs now come from the supervisor application
      origin, separate from the gateway connection. Gateway-mediated
      application routing can be turned off with `enable_gateway_service_routing`
      (default `true`). Users of the app listener must replace
      `domain` with `base_url`, deploy matching gateway, driver and
      supervisor images, and recreate existing dedicated sandbox
      pods with the new supervisor image.
    - Repository references and links now point to `ai-openshell/openshell`
      after the repository transfer.
  * Bug Fixes
    - Sandboxed workloads can now set their own CPU affinity, nice
      value and resource limits, signal themselves and queue signals,
      like in a plain container. Calls targeting processes outside
      the workload's own thread group are still denied.
    - HTTP clients (including JSON-RPC and MCP) are now promptly
      notified when an upstream closes an idle connection. Proxy
      failures before a response starts now return `502 Bad Gateway`
      with a request ID.
    - Request inspection and authorization now use the protocol
      chosen by the matching route, so overlapping routes and RPC/MCP
      requests get the right decision.
    - Clients that cache DNS answers can open new connections after
      a policy DNS mapping expires; the destination is refreshed
      and re-checked before connecting.
    - Restarting a sandbox no longer sometimes marks it as `Error`
      (`ContainerExited`) while it is still starting.
    - On multi-replica gateways, attaching to a sandbox whose main
      process has finished no longer fails with `sandbox is not</comment>
    <requestid>1400512</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
